DESCRIPTION:End of Week 9 (Oct 12-18). Post-M2 sprint.\n\nYTC: Revenue growing. Track MoM improvement.\nAlphaStream: If unlocked, assess resource needs vs portfolio burn cap.
CATEGORIES:Portfolio Pilot,Review
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pp-week10-end@appdev.local
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:📋 Week 10 End — Pulse Review
DESCRIPTION:End of Week 10 (Oct 19-25). Weekly pulse review.\n\nAll three lanes (YTC/Studio/B-GAE) should be in steady state.\nBegin M3 gate criteria pre-check.
CATEGORIES:Portfolio Pilot,Review
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pp-week11-end@appdev.local
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:📋 Week 11 End — Pulse Review
DESCRIPTION:End of Week 11 (Oct 26 - Nov 1). Pre-M3 final prep.\n\nConfirm all M3 gate criteria are on track.\nPrepare decision log documentation.\nSchedule Aegis governance review session.
CATEGORIES:Portfolio Pilot,Review
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pp-m3-gate@appdev.local
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:🔴 M3 FINAL GATE — 12-Week Assessment
DESCRIPTION:Milestone 3 Final Gate Review (end of Week 12 — Nov 2-8).\n\nFinal assessment criteria:\n✅ YTC: Consistent revenue — primary funding engine validated\n✅ YTC: 4+ monetization channels operational\n✅ Studio: 20%+ turnaround improvement sustained over 12 weeks\n✅ Studio: Direct revenue (mixing/editing) generating secondary income\n✅ B-GAE: Pilot concept finalized and grant application(s) submitted\n✅ B-GAE: At least 1 grant response received or pending\n✅ AlphaStream: Go/No-Go for full activation (if funded)\n✅ Burn: $500/mo cap maintained throughout all 12 weeks\n\nOutcomes:\n• PASS: Move to Phase 2 (YTC scale + Studio commercial + AlphaStream activation)\n• PARTIAL: Extend sprint 4 weeks with adjusted targets\n• FAIL: Aegis escalation, portfolio restructure\n\nDecision log required. Full Aegis governance review.
CATEGORIES:Portfolio Pilot,Gate Review
PRIORITY:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pp-alphastream-decision@appdev.local
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:🧠 AlphaStream — Full Activation Decision
DESCRIPTION:AlphaStream hold window ends — full activation decision.\n\nDecision context:\n• Hold intentionally placed until Portfolio Pilot Option 1 gates clear\n• Unblocks as non-dilutive funding source if YTC revenue signals materialize\n• Docker requirement noted as blocker for full stack; API-only mode available on port 8080\n\nIf YTC revenue sustained through M3: evaluate AlphaStream budget allocation for Phase 2.\nDo NOT activate if burn cap would be breached.
CATEGORIES:AlphaStream,Milestone
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pp-90day-checkpoint@appdev.local
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:📊 Portfolio Pilot — 90-Day Full Checkpoint
DESCRIPTION:Comprehensive 90-day portfolio review.\n\nAgenda:\n1. YTC revenue summary (total earned, growth rate, MoM)\n2. Studio production metrics (turnaround time, throughput, direct revenue)\n3. B-GAE status (grants submitted/awarded, pilot readiness)\n4. AlphaStream activation decision (if not already resolved at M3)\n5. Phase 2 planning kick-off\n6. Budget reconciliation ($500/mo cap review)\n7. Runway projection update (was 26 months as of May 2026)\n\nDeliverable: Phase 2 plan draft with updated allocation percentages.
CATEGORIES:Portfolio Pilot,Checkpoint
PRIORITY:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT

